{
  "slug": "obsidian-vault-for-claude-code",
  "name": "Obsidian Vault For Claude Code",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Archives your Claude Code sessions into a persistent, on-disk knowledge wiki\nthat Claude reads back in future sessions — like long-term memory, but\ninspectable, git-versioned, and split between a global vault (~/claude-vault/)\nand per-project vaults (docs/vault/) committed alongside your code. A\nSessionStart hook auto-scans finished transcripts; slash commands bootstrap\nand ingest them into atomic markdown pages with YAML frontmatter and\nwiki-links. Output is plain Markdown — Obsidian the app is optional but\nrecommended for graph view. Built on the LLM-Wiki pattern\n(RAW → WIKI ← SCHEMA) by Selma Kocabıyık.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill** and **10 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `vault` (Hybrid knowledge vault system (Obsidian-compatible markdown wikis) that archives Claude Code sessions, architectural decisions, bugs, domain concepts, entities,…)\n- **Commands** (10): `auto-ingest` (Enable, disable, or check the auto-ingest setting in vault-config.json), `batch-ingest` (Process all pending Claude Code sessions in sequence, up to a configurable maximum per run), `doctor`, `help` (List all vault slash commands with one-line descriptions and usage hints), `ingest` (Ingest the next pending Claude Code session into the appropriate vault (global or project)), `init` (Bootstrap a project vault — docs/vault/ skeleton + customized CLAUDE.md tailored to the current project), `scan` (Scan ~/.claude/projects for new Claude Code sessions and update the vault's pending-ingest queue), `skip` (Mark a pending session as skipped so it no longer appears in the ingest queue), and 2 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install obsidian-vault-for-claude-code@claude-community` from `mehmetcakoglu/claude-obsidian-vault-skill` (`plugins/vault`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
